{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve for \\(a_{100}\\) given the recurrence relation \\(a_n = \\frac{a_{n-1}}{1 + a_{n-1}}\\) and the initial condition \\(a_0 = 6\\), we will first investigate the behavior of the sequence by calculating the first few terms and then look for a pattern.\n\nStarting with \\(a_0 = 6\\):\n\n\\[a_1 = \\frac{a_0}{1 + a_0} = \\frac{6}{1 + 6} = \\frac{6}{7}\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\(a_2\\):\n\n\\[a_2 = \\frac{a_1}{1 + a_1} = \\frac{\\frac{6}{7}}{1 + \\frac{6}{7}} = \\frac{\\frac{6}{7}}{\\frac{13}{7}} = \\frac{6}{13}\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\(a_3\\):\n\n\\[a_3 = \\frac{a_2}{1 + a_2} = \\frac{\\frac{6}{13}}{1 + \\frac{6}{13}} = \\frac{\\frac{6}{13}}{\\frac{19}{13}} = \\frac{6}{19}\\]\n\nFrom these calculations, we observe that the sequence appears to be of the form \\(a_n = \\frac{6}{6n + 1}\\). We will now prove this by induction.\n\n","prefix_end":789,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,369,17767,64,15159,16,15,15,11035,8,2661,279,75193,12687,17767,64,1089,284,1124,37018,90,64,15159,77,12,16,3417,90,16,488,264,15159,77,12,16,3417,57758,323,279,2856,2971,17767,64,62,15,284,220,21,59,701,582,686,1156,19314,279,7709,315,279,8500,553,37614,279,1156,2421,3793,323,1221,1401,369,264,5383,382,24617,448,17767,64,62,15,284,220,21,59,7731,78045,64,62,16,284,1124,37018,90,64,62,15,15170,16,488,264,62,15,92,284,1124,37018,90,21,15170,16,488,220,21,92,284,1124,37018,90,21,15170,22,11035,2533,5847,11,582,11047,17767,64,62,17,59,7731,78045,64,62,17,284,1124,37018,90,64,62,16,15170,16,488,264,62,16,92,284,1124,37018,35702,37018,90,21,15170,22,3417,90,16,488,1124,37018,90,21,15170,22,3417,284,1124,37018,35702,37018,90,21,15170,22,3417,35702,37018,90,16,18,15170,22,3417,284,1124,37018,90,21,15170,16,18,11035,2533,5847,11,582,11047,17767,64,62,18,59,7731,78045,64,62,18,284,1124,37018,90,64,62,17,15170,16,488,264,62,17,92